    {
      "id": "claim_e8973ed446a34cf8be5a748bb35e59ae",
      "statement": "A failed pipeline still writes a value into Redis under the request ID with the normal TTL: runPipelineAsync catches any exception, stores ERROR_PREFIX ('Error: ') plus the message before rethrowing ArdocoException, so the key is an error marker rather than absent. On retrieval, getResultFromDatabase throws ArdocoException (HTTP 500 via GlobalExceptionHandler) when the stored value starts with the prefix, versus IllegalArgumentException (422) for a missing key; within the TTL window a repeated identical start request therefore hits the cached branch and surfaces the failure as 500 instead of re-running.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java#L71-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d65f6668d7b12691e9f452e8a3e9dfce2329deaf26027fa128e7045951519b2:"
        },
        {
