        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractService.java#L58-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7fcce0349951b76b7e1d7130350be586c8f3a553ef4af22fa5c6a0d6f71708b0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8cd8738603b41989eb9591ee89d23af",
      "statement": "The rethrown ArdocoException of a failed run is observed asymmetrically by the two start endpoints: /start never consumes the future, so the failure surfaces only later through the Redis error marker on retrieval, while /start-and-wait is blocked on the future in ResultService.waitForResult and receives the exceptional completion as an ExecutionException rethrown as ArdocoException (immediate 500).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/AbstractController.java#L85-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ce1064759aba171c39e1f1017130f8fedd7119d18efeb00ecb7b43505b69306:"
