          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ea2f7a987e7f38ddcecd0c492e072e7a8fa98b832496a363be2094bb080ad45:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8699168a5f7f4e7fb0a6725cc4db1dc6",
      "statement": "The finally block in runPipelineAsync runs on success, failure, and interruption and always removes the request ID from the in-flight registry and deletes every temp input file, so no registry entry outlives its future's terminal state and dispatched runs never leak the temp files created during request shaping.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/service/AbstractRunnerTLRService.java#L119-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:432d1e6ba60a0311e99b5d4874e57227cd1afc73227d5a94ecebeab1ee27e6b2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5cabd3a8fc324e9aa7c9456bf4ad26a3",
      "statement": "The finally-block cleanup only covers dispatched runs: if the request thread fails between temp-file conversion and dispatch — for example runner.setUp throwing IOException while creating the per-request temp output directory — the already-written temp input files are not deleted by any application code, and the runner's temp output directory is never deleted either (the only delete call site is the input-file loop in runPipelineAsync).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/tlr/rest/api/controller/ArDoCodeController.java#L141-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2591489db94770a6977146ecb8a4e630930ae7db11305f4370c7ac6789358926:"
