      "statement": "handleRunPipelineAndWaitForResult waits only when runPipeline returned empty, blocking up to tlr.timeout.seconds (60 seconds by default); a result arriving in time yields 200 with the payload, a timeout yields 202 Accepted with the 'timed out — try querying only the result using the projectId' message, and if the run finished between the two service calls waitForResult finds the registry empty and reads the result from Redis directly.",
